# File: tests/features/convert_smoke_repository_to_a_python_sdlc_host.feature
# Generated from: specs/35-convert-smoke-repository-to-a-python-sdlc-host/requirements.md
Feature: Convert smoke repository to a Python SDLC host
  As a nmg-sdlc operator exercising the toolkit against a disposable host repository
  I want this repository converted from copied Node.js plugin contents into a minimal production-shaped Python project
  So that the complete nmg-sdlc issue to spec to execute workflow can be run against a deterministic, cross-platform, independently verifiable Python host

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Installable greeting happy path
    Given the repository is an installable Python distribution nmg-sdlc-smoke-python with import package nmg_sdlc_smoke requiring Python 3.12+
    When a caller invokes greet with Ada
    Then the function returns exactly Hello, Ada

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Console script happy path
    Given the distribution is installed with its console script
    When nmg-smoke Ada is run
    Then the process exits 0 and prints Hello, Ada followed by a single newline

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Blank name is rejected
    Given a blank or whitespace-only name
    When greet is called or nmg-smoke is invoked with that name
    Then the library raises ValueError and the CLI exits non-zero without printing a greeting

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Independent Python verification
    Given a clean checkout on macOS, Linux, or Windows
    When pytest, pytest-bdd features under tests/features/, and Ruff are run
    Then every acceptance criterion has a Gherkin scenario, those commands exit 0, and results do not depend on machine-specific paths

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Python CI replaces plugin verification
    Given a pull request or a push to main
    When GitHub Actions Python CI is inspected
    Then it installs the project, runs pytest including tests/features/, and runs Ruff on Python 3.12
    And the Node plugin workflows nmg-sdlc-verify.yml, skill-inventory-audit.yml, and sync-marketplace-pointer.yml are absent

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Clean cutover preserves SDLC delivery contracts
    Given the converted working tree
    When it is inspected
    Then copied plugin runtime workflows/, agents/, commands/, Node scripts/, OMP package.json, src/extension.ts, other plugin specs/, and live smoke marker files are gone
    And LICENSE, 3.x VERSION synced to pyproject.toml, CHANGELOG history, the managed contribution gate, the managed issue form, and the AGENTS.md spec-context markers remain

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Python-focused steering and contribution guidance
    Given a contributor opening README, CONTRIBUTING, AGENTS, and steering
    When they read current guidance
    Then the documents describe this Python SDLC smoke host with src layout, pytest, pytest-bdd, Ruff, and VERSION synchronized with pyproject.toml
    And they do not describe an Oh My Pi plugin as the current product
